WEBVTT

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.600
"Shinkansen"
"Carriage 1: Vault Car"

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:16.430
Well, I guess this means
we're done with the job.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:20.470
Thanks for all the fun, guys. Later.

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.970
Where are you going?

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:26.350
I'm heading back to Kansai
to whoop that Executioner's ass.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.180
Huh? You almost died!

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.470
Can you not let my first aid go to waste?

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.600
Besides, you still haven't got your billion.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.810
Hah! Money means nothing to me.
You guys can have it.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:42.850
Nobody's ever scared me like that before.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:45.810
I'll beat him, even if it kills me!

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.680
But dying isn't winning!

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.020
Who's gonna die?!

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:50.770
You are!

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:55.680
Ms. Swindler, you just gotta
let Bro follow his heart.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:56.520
Huh?

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.850
That's just the way he rolls.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.520
I think you just don't wanna die.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:07.430
Th-That's not true! B-Bro, I'll just be
in the way if I go with you, right?

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:08.600
Nah, c'mon!

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.140
I done goofed!

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:14.350
I'm afraid you're all mistaken.
The job isn't over yet.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.100
--Huh?
--You shittin' me?

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.560
We got you outta the damn vault.
Like hell it ain't!

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:23.060
Were you not listening
during the hotel briefing?

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:27.220
The job is to deliver us to a certain location.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.720
We're not there yet.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.390
I don't give a damn about any of that.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:36.810
I see that. But our destination
is located in Kansai.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:41.720
Since you're returning there,
we may as well go together.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:43.100
Oh?

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.390
Where in Kansai? What's the destination?

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:49.270
I'll tell you when we're out of here.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.720
"Absolute Quarantine Zone"
"Outside Shinkansen Carriage 3"

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.310
Hacker?

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:05.810
I'm going ahead to Kanto.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:09.100
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:12.890
Didn't you hear what
Mr. Black Cat said on the train?

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:13.890
All of it.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:20.140
Then, why? If you keep going,
you'll die in the Decontamination Zone!

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:24.310
Even so, this is a huge chance for me.

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:29.930
Can you imagine what it's like
to feel bored, no matter what?

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:35.390
I've tried to find things to entertain myself,
but nothing is ever enough.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:38.850
But it might be different in Kanto.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.520
It might be a world that doesn't bore me.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.680
Every single day might be
fresh and fun in its own way.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.140
That's why I'm going to Kanto.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.220
But you can't--

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:56.560
I'm sick and tired of living
in this boring-ass world.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.020
I'm taking this chance,
even if it costs my life.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:03.270
You're kidding!
Where there's life, there's hope!

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:07.180
Hacker, are you forgetting
about the collar bomb?

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.720
Your hacking abilities will come in handy if--

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:15.640
It took a while to figure it out.
That's Kanto-made stuff for you.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.220
--Take mine off, too!
--This is why I hate kids.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:19.020
--The hell? Not fair!
--What a waste!

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:23.390
But what's the point if you really end up dead?

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:36.770
Here's a parting gift. You wanted one, right?

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:43.100
But parting gifts are for the people leaving.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.350
I'll return this someday!

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.680
"Akudama Drive"

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.470
Looks like you're finally up.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.020
Master...

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:42.600
Thank the recovery crew. A few minutes
later and we'd be in a grave.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:47.060
No... There'd be nothing
left of us to fill a grave.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:50.350
The Akudama!

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.270
What about them?!

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:54.350
What happened to them?!

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.310
"Kansai Police Hospital"
"West Building Room 603"

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:57.310
They were on the <i>Shinkansen </i>heading
for the Decontamination Zone.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:59.180
They were on the <i>Shinkansen </i>heading
for the Decontamination Zone.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:00.470
That's all I know.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:03.270
I see.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:06.770
In that case, they've gotta be dead.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:11.890
The Akudama are alive.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:13.180
You're kidding!

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.390
"Kansai Special Communication Room"
"Sky Hall"

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.390
You failed to deal with them.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:19.220
But there's no way they could have survived.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:24.310
It's true. You have blundered greatly this time.

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:25.930
Right!

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:31.970
Something that was supposed to be
delivered to Kanto was stolen as well.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:33.720
You're on thin ice.

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.930
Yes, sir. I will keep that in mind.

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:49.270
"Near the Absolute Quarantine Zone"
"Abandoned Ward 3"

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:03.020
The hell? We got out of that shithole
and now it's raining?

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:06.600
I hate rain. It makes my hair all stiff.

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:11.640
Man, it's pretty awesome we got
outta there with that barrier, yeah?

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:14.220
Huh? Yeah...

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:16.060
Got anything else cool?

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:20.770
Like a bazooka to blow up the
Executioners or a money tree?!

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:24.770
We don't have anything that can be used to kill.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:27.020
We didn't have time to prepare.

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:28.220
Hmm?

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:33.470
Tell us the destination already.
Not all of us wanna sit around all day.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:36.970
You're so impatient when
it comes to work, Courier.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:40.930
Fine, I will. Our destination is--

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:43.220
Before that...

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:45.850
It's about time you come clean.

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:49.810
Who the hell are you guys?

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:53.470
Is that necessary to know for the job?

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:59.930
That's right. The job we accepted
was to steal and deliver a vault.

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:03.560
But instead, we're delivering children.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:07.060
Even you should know that changes things.

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:12.100
Then I'll pay more for the job.
I can double it if you want.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.270
For real?!

00:08:13.270 --> 00:08:17.640
Regardless of the situation,
I'm still your employer.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:24.020
Damn kids. Did you honestly think
we took this job just for the reward?

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.180
Hmm?

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:26.720
--I thought the dreadlocked gorilla
and Hacker made that clear.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.180
--Are gorillas strong?
--I thought the dreadlocked gorilla
and Hacker made that clear.

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:29.520
--Huh? Yeah.
--I thought the dreadlocked gorilla
and Hacker made that clear.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:32.890
You're not gonna keep us hooked with money.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:37.350
These collar bombs mean nothing
if we can't trust you.

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:40.180
A smart boy like you should get that.

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:43.970
Now, answer me. Who the hell are you?

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:49.770
What do you think you're doing?

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.180
I think that's enough.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:54.810
I'm sure they can't say for a reason.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:58.270
I mean, they <i>were </i>in a vault on the <i>Shinkansen</i>.

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:01.520
That's exactly why we need to know.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.810
Somehow or another, they're involved with Kanto.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:10.430
This is way beyond stealing some vault.
Kanto won't keep quiet.

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:15.520
And if that happens, won't it be
a problem for you, Swindler?

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:17.680
Hey! Lemme join if you're fighting!

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:20.180
Now's not the time, Bro!

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:27.470
Hey, did you hear what I said?

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:30.390
Um... This...

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:31.930
What?

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:35.390
I think you're being a bully.

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:36.180
Huh?

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.020
Hmm?

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:42.310
You're trying to force answers out of little
kids when they're not ready to talk!

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.350
That's plain bullying!

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.970
Beautiful...

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:52.470
Truly, so beautiful...

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:55.600
Bullying is bad. Cut it out, Doc.

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.180
Listen to Bro, Doc!

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.850
Want me to sever your carotid?

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:01.520
We're wasting time.

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:05.770
Keep all your damn feelings
out of the way of work.

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:07.220
Courier...

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:12.560
I finish 100% of the jobs I take,
even ones from damn kids.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:16.350
Now, what's the destination?
I'll take you there.

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:22.350
I guess you're taking them no matter what.
Whatever. Suit yourself.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.720
It appears we're on the same page now.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:26.310
"Workbook"

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.930
What do these numbers mean?

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:32.970
They're coordinates.

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:38.850
These coordinates are our
destination... Expo Park.

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:42.470
Expo Park, you said?

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:46.310
--♬ Rain drops rain drops brighten my day! ♬
--Expo Park? Was there a place
like that in Kansai?

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:47.350
--♬ Rain drops rain drops brighten my day! ♬
--I like how "Expo" rolls off the
tongue. Sounds tough!

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:49.810
--♬ Mom under the umbrella watches me play! ♬
--I like how "Expo" rolls off the
tongue. Sounds tough!

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:51.770
--♬ Mom under the umbrella watches me play! ♬
--Where is it? Got a map?

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:52.890
--♬ Splish splash splish splash la la la! ♬
--I know where.

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:55.220
--♬ Splish splash splish splash la la la! ♬
--With just the coordinates? Whoa!

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:58.180
--♬ Splish splash splish splash la la la! ♬
--But I don't know what these last six digits are.

00:10:58.180 --> 00:10:59.680
What are they?

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.020
You'll find out.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:03.600
This kid is always hiding something.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:07.560
Could you maybe cut him a little slack please?

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:12.270
I'm starving. Let's find something to eat.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:14.680
There ain't nothing to eat for miles.

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:17.140
I haven't eaten in ages.

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:22.060
If you're taking us to Expo Park,
we can provide some food.

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:26.850
You have food? Oh, I guess
it's kinda yours though.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.060
Huh? It's empty.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:30.810
Close the lid and say what you want.

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:34.310
Huh? Um...

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:35.640
<i>Takoyaki</i>!

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:37.270
Open it up.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:41.520
--H-Huh?! What is this, magic?!
--Whoa!

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:47.930
This lunch box can reconfigure atoms
in the water and air to make food.

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:50.520
It has 50 items on the menu.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.770
Professor had us take it
so we wouldn't get hungry.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:56.430
Professor? What a nice person!

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:59.680
Hmm? I don't know if they're nice or not.

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:01.720
Um, is this Professor person--?

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:03.600
If this makes food, I want meat!

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:05.100
--Gimme meat!
--Whoa!

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:13.890
The weaker one is, the more
they try to take by force.

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:17.100
Okay, Swindler! I'll just wait till you're done!

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:19.180
--After all, I'm strong!
--What a simpleton.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:21.810
--Yes, you are. How nice of you.
--He's a total idiot.

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:25.680
Whoa! Look at all this meat!

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.890
At least one of us is classy.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:35.220
I just love how fluffy they are!

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:38.180
Huh? Where the hell is my ramen?!

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:39.810
It doesn't do soup.

00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:41.560
The box would get dirty.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:44.220
Didn't it just do wine?!

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:53.430
Will marshmallows fill you up?

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:57.310
They're better when they're bloody
and look like brains!

00:12:57.310 --> 00:12:58.060
Wha--?

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:00.020
--I want more!
--That was fast!

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:05.350
So you like <i>takoyaki </i>then?
You had some when we first met.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:09.890
Tastes better than other
shitty food. But just barely.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:13.560
Your mouth is stuffed like a hamster.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:18.060
You guys should eat. That's why
Professor gave it to you, right?

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:22.100
Yeah. But we're fine without eating.

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:24.310
I don't know what I want to eat.

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:26.560
Huh? You're not hungry?

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:29.720
I feel an empty stomach, but no hunger.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:30.890
Hmm?

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.640
Open wide, you two!

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:39.850
Huh? There's no point...

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:41.520
Hey! Mmf!

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:45.060
Tasty?

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:49.140
I don't know... but...

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.180
Yeah?

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:54.810
My tummy... is warm.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:59.020
Is this another swindler trick?

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:02.310
The only ones it would fool are you two.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:10.720
Hello! Bunny here!

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.430
'Sup?! It's Shark here!

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:16.350
Hey, everyone! Were you looking
forward to the program?

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:19.770
Shark, hey, Shark! You know about Kyushu Plant?

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:26.140
I know it's an experiment facility run by Kanto,
but that's everything I know!

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:30.060
Then since you live under a rock,
I'll teach you all about it!

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:31.600
Lucky me!

00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:37.720
Kyushu Plant researches and
manufactures stuff that Kanto wants!

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:38.850
Yeah?

00:14:38.850 --> 00:14:43.430
Every single thing labeled
"Kanto-made" is created there!

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:47.810
That's incredible!
Is there anything they can't make?

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:49.720
They can make anything!

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:52.810
And I mean anything!

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:57.140
I wish I had some Kanto-made brains!

00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:58.970
That'd be perfect for you!

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:01.140
Yeah! You got that right!

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:03.350
Well, until next time!

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:06.770
"The End"
"Produced by
Kansai"

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:12.310
You're better than I imagined.

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:14.470
Seems we have devil's luck.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:17.680
Boss, I'm sorry you had to come all this way.

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:20.600
So? I know you didn't come to visit.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:22.220
You're a smart one.

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:25.720
Please keep it short since we're in pain here.

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:30.680
If you're well enough to joke,
I won't hold back any punches.

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:31.520
Huh?

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:36.680
You failed to deal with the Akudama twice--
at the hotel and on the <i>Shinkansen</i>.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:39.390
This is absolutely inexcusable.

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:43.100
Um, didn't they die on the <i>Shinkansen</i>?

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:45.220
The Akudama are alive.

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:48.890
No way! They escaped the
Absolute Quarantine Zone?!

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:53.140
What's more, they stole goods
from the front carriage.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:56.680
They achieved their objective alive and well.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.890
You're kidding...

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:04.890
Unless your brain stopped working,
you should know what that means.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.430
Utter defeat.

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:07.350
Huh?

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:08.770
Is it not?

00:16:08.770 --> 00:16:13.640
That's right. This is the biggest
failure since our inception.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:17.310
We've received orders directly from Kanto.

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:21.100
We're to do a full-scale
search-and-destroy mission.

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:24.310
Boss, give us another chance! We won't--

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:26.560
Know your place!

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:32.220
You two are hereby suspended.
Be grateful you're still alive.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:41.520
Master, let's do something on our own.
We can't let it end like this!

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.720
We've been suspended. Orders are orders.

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:48.140
But we were supposed to kill those Akudama!

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:50.430
Shouldn't we take responsibility?!

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:52.720
You don't know what you're saying.

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:57.180
Listen, we failed twice. End of story.

00:16:57.180 --> 00:17:00.810
We got off easy with a suspension. Be grateful.

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:03.100
No way...

00:17:03.100 --> 00:17:06.060
Master, you're fine with this?

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:15.140
So, I guess we're returning
to Kansai. What's the plan?

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:16.850
Run straight in and kick ass!

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:18.850
Eat your meat before it rots.

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:19.970
Whoops!

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:24.310
The Executioners should know
by now that we're still alive.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:29.020
In which case, they probably
set up a dragnet to find us.

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:34.270
We'll sneak in through the drainage pipe
for the moat around Kansai.

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:36.100
From the north side?

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:42.680
It's a shortcut to the coordinates.
I'll take them there no matter what.

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:44.220
We leave in four hours.

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:45.640
Not right away?

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:48.220
Woohoo! I can take a nap!

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:52.350
I'll sleep, too.
I can kill a bunch in my dreams.

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:54.100
Hey.

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:56.930
Yeah? Wh-What is it?

00:17:56.930 --> 00:18:00.430
I got to see the way you sway people's hearts.

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:02.350
Huh?

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:07.430
Don't let your guard down.
Your little innocent act won't work on me.

00:18:07.430 --> 00:18:09.600
That's not what I--

00:18:21.770 --> 00:18:23.310
Help me...!

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:35.970
How long will you tag along?

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:37.930
Huh?

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:40.140
Courier...

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:45.560
How long? I wanna take them
all the way to Expo Park.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:48.970
I can't let kids that little
go off on their own.

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:52.890
In any case, it's not like
I have much of a choice.

00:18:58.310 --> 00:19:03.520
Say, is there anything you value
more than your own life?

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:05.100
What do you mean?

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:10.100
For example, what if you had to
give up your life to finish this job?

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:14.640
Like, if you could run away and live,
what would you do?

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:18.560
That's a shitty question...
because I never fail.

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:23.270
Penny for your thoughts?
Oh, speaking of which...

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:24.430
Here.

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:28.930
I'm giving back the 500 yen you
dropped at the <i>takoyaki </i>place.

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.470
Nope. Dropped money's bad luck.

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:36.560
C'mon, just take it!
This 500 yen got me into this mess--!

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:37.390
Mmm?

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:39.020
Forget it. Just take it.

00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:42.720
Nope. I only take money when accepting a job.

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:45.520
Ugh, so stubborn! Take it!

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:47.060
---Nope
---Take it already!

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:49.020
--Nope.
--Hey! Where are you going?!

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:51.680
Lemme pay you back!

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.890
To all Executioners!

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:06.680
As of now, I'm declaring a
search-and-destroy of seven Akudama!

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:12.310
They attacked the <i>Shinkansen</i>
and stole goods bound for Kanto!

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:15.520
This is a disgrace to all Executioners!

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:17.890
What is our duty?

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:21.890
To exterminate all Akudama scum from the world!

00:20:21.890 --> 00:20:24.220
Do we let them do as they please?

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:26.890
No! We won't stand for it!

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:29.140
"Wanted" "Dead or Alive"

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:29.140
Executioners must be the ultimate threat!
Executioners must be the enforcers of justice!

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:34.220
Executioners must be the ultimate threat!
Executioners must be the enforcers of justice!

00:20:34.220 --> 00:20:39.310
We must cull and cut them down
without rest until none remain!

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:42.220
We will take every one of their lives!

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:46.680
And then we'll display their
severed heads to set an example!

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:50.850
As Executioners, that is
the purpose of our existence!

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:54.600
An order to all Executioners...

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:58.060
Dammit! To think we can do nothing!

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:01.100
Master! I can't stand this!

00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:04.560
Master?

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:07.220
Are you sleeping?

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:11.060
Master? Pardon me.

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:12.220
Wha...?

00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:24.060
"Execution Department HQ"
"Monument Hall"

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:37.060
Is this the entrance you were talking about?

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:38.180
Yeah. It'll take us all the way to Takatsuki.

00:21:38.180 --> 00:21:40.810
"Outside Kansai"
"Fortification Wall  North Side"

00:21:38.180 --> 00:21:40.810
Yeah. It'll take us all the way to Takatsuki.

00:21:40.810 --> 00:21:41.600
"Outside Kansai"
"Fortification Wall  North Side"

00:21:40.810 --> 00:21:41.600
Courier's secret route, huh?

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:43.810
Courier's secret route, huh?

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:47.060
Isn't the smell just awful?

00:21:47.060 --> 00:21:49.430
It smells like Kansai's toilet.

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:50.390
--I think it smells like meat.

00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:51.270
--I should make deodorizer.
--I think it smells like meat.

00:21:51.270 --> 00:21:53.020
--I should make deodorizer.
--Maybe rotten meat.

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:56.140
The kids can ride on my bike. I'll take 'em--

00:21:58.060 --> 00:22:01.390
You thought you got away from me?

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:46.970
He made his decision. He's prepared to die.
